  "_approach": "The 'rewind' moment on a 32nd grid: bar 1 keeps the 2-step kick and clap while the snare enters in 16ths from beat 3; bar 2 drops the kick, the snare tightens to 32nds through beats 3-4 with velocity ramping to 127, and the last two 32nds are left empty as the silence gap before the drop. Ref: DJ EZ-style live reload builds, Todd Edwards 'Saved My Life' cut-up turnarounds.",
